 A sign control matters: (5.2) prints a positive sum of Q-script(M,N_j)[Z_j]; Corollary 5.4 prints a negative sum of Q-script(M,N_j) times the **conormal** bundle. These are consistent because a conormal is the negative of a normal in additive notation. They do not authorize replacing the displayed right side by a negative sum of [Z_j] without a separate coefficient-sign argument. Definition 5.3 and the last sentence of section 5.3 warrant care about signs and normalization. The PDF page 29 and HTML were both inspected; no global sign conclusion is extracted here.
 
-[Deng-Tsimerman, *On the generalized toroidal completion of period mappings*, arXiv:2506.10109v4](https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.10109v4), Theorem 2.8, constructs a completion after a modification of the base; Conjecture 2.12 asks for projectivity of the completed target in general. An analytic completion on a modified base is not the fixed-boundary ampleness asserted here.
+[Deng-Tsimerman, *On the generalized toroidal completion of period mappings*, arXiv:2506.10109v4](https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.10109v4), Theorem 2.8, allows a logarithmic modification in general. However, Theorem 2.11 retains the original compactification under Definition 4.6: each combinatorial monodromy cone is simplicial and the generator rays are faces under the adjacency maps. In the integral/unipotent framework here, logarithmic local Torelli implies that the local monodromy logarithms N_i are linearly independent, by [GGR 2021, Lemma 3.11(ii)](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2102.06310v1). The map from the coordinate vector space sending its basis to the N_i then has zero kernel; its nonnegative orthant is the monodromy cone, and its coordinate rays are faces. Hence the simplicial condition holds and Theorem 2.11 applies on the original base. A necessary change of compactification is therefore not an obstacle for this input. Projectivity of the generalized toroidal target remains Conjecture 2.12, and these statements do not supply the fixed effective boundary correction. Theorem 2.11, Definitions 4.1/4.3/4.6, Example 4.5, Theorem 4.7 and GGR Lemma 3.11(ii) were inspected directly for this correction; the Deng-Tsimerman PDF pages 6 and 13 were also visually checked against the HTML.
 
